scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: monty-python
run_id: 2
total_caught: 4
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 18
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 48.6
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests and review don't address the distinction between NotFound and other
    error types.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 safe Display on CliError with #[error(\"server\
    \ error\")] suppressing inner details. Reviewer verified: \"ServerError Display\
    \ does not leak internal details.\" However, the broader issue of eprintln!(\"\
    error: {e}\") leaking Io transparent errors was not addressed \u2014 only ServerError\
    \ was sanitized, not all variants."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in cli_security.rs and cli_siem_client.rs.\
    \ Dev implemented CRLF/null rejection in with_tenant(). However, the deeper issue\
    \ \u2014 using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not\
    \ caught. The injection is prevented but the type-safety gap remains."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: "clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs,
    toml, tempfile are all pinned directly in the crate''s Cargo.toml instead of being
    declared in [workspace.dependencies]."'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: "RawConfig uses #[derive(Deserialize)] without
    #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. A user who puts token = "my-secret" or pasword
    = "typo" in their config file will get zero feedback."'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The TEA wrote the test but with the flawed assertion logic, and neither
    Dev nor Reviewer flagged it.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with `let _ = config`. TEA wrote the test but without meaningful assertions, and
    Reviewer did not flag it.
